`.length` of a constant string or list folds to its count. html's static
page writes a non-reactive text only once it folds to a literal, so an unfolded
`.length` came out as an empty span.

deny out/none/html/index.html `<span>\s*</span>` -- every text folded to its literal
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    none {
        html()
    }
}

ui.window(title="t") {
    const greeting = "héllo"
    const xs = [1, 2, 3]
    ui.vbox {
        ui.text(value="string {greeting.length}")
        ui.text(value="list {xs.length}")
    }
}
-- out/none/html/index.html --
<!-- Code generated by sngl (html) from app.sngl; DO NOT EDIT. -->

